{
  "0": "Feature construction: scale each nonpadding input item embedding by 0.75 + 0.5 × log(1 + training_count(item))/log(1 + maximum_training_count), with counts computed separately from each category’s training interactions. This bounded frequency feature may help SASRec distinguish established preferences from rare events. Keep learned embeddings, topology, readout, loss and optimizer unchanged; persist training counts for identical inference.",
  "1": "Network architecture: replace each SASRec feed-forward block’s ReLU activation with GELU, preserving block count, attention heads, hidden widths, residual paths and causal masking. Smoother nonlinear transformations may improve optimization and capture subtle preference patterns. Keep features, embeddings, scoring, history selection, readout, loss and optimizer unchanged.",
  "2": "Sequence modeling: double the baseline maximum context length while retaining chronological order, causal masking and the most recent interactions when truncation is necessary. Longer histories may recover persistent interests in sparse purchase sequences and improve validation HR@10. Preserve positional embedding design, features, Transformer topology, readout, loss and optimizer; match context length in training and prediction.",
  "3": "Training strategy: retain the baseline optimizer and peak learning rate, but introduce linear learning-rate warmup over the first 5% of scheduled updates, followed by cosine decay to 10% of the peak by epoch 200. Gentler initial updates and gradual decay may improve convergence and ranking stability. Keep batch size, dropout, weight decay, model, features, loss, seeds and evaluation unchanged."
}
